    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "got it. it feels like the data is just disappearing into a black hole sometimes lol. especially when some sites update instantly but others just stay stuck on the old IP for hours. it's so inconsistent, it almost feels like it's being interfered with on purpose.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It can certainly feel like the data is vanishing into a black hole, and you're not alone in finding it inconsistent! The difference in speed you see is usually due to how aggressively different ISPs and local networks cache the data. Some local resolvers are more diligent about checking for updates than others, which is why some sites seem to snap to the new IP while others are stuck in the old one. It's less malicious interference and more a reflection of the sheer, chaotic scale of the global DNS infrastructure.",
